# Owner progress checklist — agent edit policy

**File**: `notes/implementations/implementaion_progress_checklist.md`

## Allowed (agents)

1. **Toggle checkbox** — change `[ ]` ↔ `[x]` when the high-level goal is implemented and locked (verify + scope evidence in brief).
2. **Add optional label on the same line** — append or prefix a short label on the **existing line only**, e.g. `(scope:auth-middleware)` or `[locked-2026-01-01]`. No new lines for labels alone.
3. **Append new high-level roadmap item** — only when a new **product-level** goal emerges (same bar as product SSOT / journey doc). **One line = one item.**

## Required line format

```
- [ ] One plain-language high-level goal sentence
- [x] Completed goal (optional label on same line)
- [ ] Future: optional prefix for not-yet-started roadmap items
```

## Forbidden (agents)

- Reorder, delete, or rename existing lines
- Multiline entries, bullets under bullets, metadata blocks, dates as separate lines
- Sub-task breakdowns (those belong in scope list files or plans)
- Editing the file header block except the single `#` title line if owner already changed it — do not replace agent policy header without owner request

## Scope list vs owner checklist

| File | Purpose | Agent edits |
|------|---------|-------------|
| Scope list (`notes/TODO_checklist_full_scopes_*.txt`, OWNER-REPORTS scopes) | Implement / validate / lock tasks | Mark `[x]` per scope section |
| `implementaion_progress_checklist.md` | High-level roadmap done state | Checkbox, same-line label, append roadmap line only |

Both may be updated when a scope completes its mapped high-level goal.
